  "docTitle": "Video Conferencing (Zoom / Teams Meetings) - SDE Prep Dojo",
  "description": "Design a Zoom or Microsoft Teams style video meeting service: WebRTC, mesh vs SFU vs MCU, NAT traversal with STUN/TURN, simulcast and SVC, cascaded SFUs across regions, failover and recording.",
  "hero": {
    "tag": "header",
    "attrs": {
      "class": "page-hero"
    },
    "html": "\n        <div class=\"hero-meta\">\n          <span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"5\">Level 5 - Interview-ready</span>\n          <span class=\"time\">40 min</span>\n          <span class=\"chip company\">Microsoft</span><span class=\"chip company\">Amazon</span>\n        </div>\n        <h1>Video Conferencing (Zoom / Teams Meetings)</h1>\n        <p class=\"lead\">Design a meeting service where millions of people see and hear each other with less than a third of a second of delay: how media really flows (WebRTC over UDP), why the server forwards instead of mixing (SFU), how calls get through home routers and office firewalls (STUN/TURN), and how one meeting stretches across continents without breaking.</p>\n      "
